## Interface: 11200
# ^ WoW vanilla 1.12 client (Lua 5.0). This is the vanilla port of the addon;
#   the Classic Era 1.15 variant lives in addon/WowMobile.
## Title: WoW Mobile (Vanilla)
## Notes: Portrait touch UI overhaul for streaming WoW 1.12 to a phone — lives in the centered 9:16 band of a native landscape window (band layout, the 1.12 default) or fills a portrait window; 1080x1920 design space, world square + control deck.
## Author: WoW Mobile project
## Version: 0.4.3
## SavedVariables: WowMobileDB

# Load order is the dependency order: Core provides the namespace/bus/timers,
# Band the landscape-band mode decision + the anchor frame the whole layout
# hangs off (it must precede every WM.Px consumer, since the px factor is
# computed against the band width — band layout is the server default for
# 1.12 clients), Config the saved variables, Blizzard the default-UI
# banishment, Viewport the world square and deck rect (anchored to the band
# frame), Deck the panel/scroller/menu infrastructure,
# MoveMode the long-press pickup/drop layer (its MakeTarget/Begin*/Drop* API
# must exist before the bar and panel modules register their cells as drop
# targets). Bar and HUD modules then stack bottom-up inside the deck (each
# anchors to the frame the previous module published in WM.Layout; Pet also
# anchors its status strip to the unit row UnitFrames publishes), and the
# panel modules only depend on Deck (+ MoveMode). LootSheet and RollFrames
# replace the banished LootFrame/GroupLootFrames and depend only on Deck.
# The economy sheets (Bank, Mail, Trade, AuctionHouse, Crafting) replace the
# Blizzard frames banished in Blizzard.lua and depend on Deck + MoveMode
# (plus Core's money-stepper/edit-box/confirm-overlay widgets).
# The social/system set (round 3): Raid and Social are deck panels reached by
# long-press on the bottom row (Deck.lua) — Raid also depends on UnitFrames'
# boosted-dropdown wrap (WM.OpenUnitMenu); Stable and Reader are event-opened
# bottom sheets replacing PetStableFrame/ItemTextFrame (banished in
# Blizzard.lua); Inspect replaces the global InspectUnit launcher so the
# target menu's Inspect opens its panel. All depend only on Deck (+ Core).
# WorldMap reflows Blizzard's map over the deck; Talents reflows the LoD
# Blizzard_TalentUI TalentFrame into the world square (installed on
# ADDON_LOADED, since 1.12 loads it via TalentFrame_LoadUI on first open).
# Settings loads last because its panel
# drives Config + Viewport. (No Compat.lua in this port: the 1.12 API is
# called directly.)
